.TH UNLINK 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
unlink \- remove a filesystem entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "int unlink(const char* " path ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR unlink ()
removes the named non\-directory entry. A symbolic link itself is removed,
not its target. An open file remains accessible through existing descriptors
after its last name is removed, until those descriptors are closed.
Use
.BR rmdir (3crunch)
for an empty directory.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Zero on success, leaving
.B errno
unchanged; \-1 on failure with
.B errno
set to the positive Linux error number.
.SH ERRORS
Possible errors include
.BR ENOENT ,
.BR EACCES ,
.BR EISDIR ,
and
.BR EROFS .
Other Linux
.BR unlink (2)
errors are possible.
.SH NOTES
Include
.B <errno.h>
for error constants. Crunch
.B errno
is process\-wide, not thread\-local.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rmdir (3crunch),
.BR rename (3crunch),
.BR unlink (2)
